2026-09-27T07:55:58.2031053Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2031528Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2032063Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2032499Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2032704Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2033277Z ================
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2033497Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2033801Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2034456Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2034925Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2035108Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2035597Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2035899Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2036178Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2036798Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2037421Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2038540Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2039554Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2039739Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2040457Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2041350Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2041815Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2042403Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2043076Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2043281Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2043690Z ========
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2043899Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2046352Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2048845Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2049487Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2050092Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2051480Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2052628Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2053580Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2054432Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2055165Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2055368Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2056525Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2056811Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2058695Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2061092Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2062235Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2063949Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:55:58.2064383Z 
